// NOT the first player-authored StaticAura -- checked before writing this:
// assets/common/abilities/spells/transmutation/plant_growth.ron already
// ships StaticAura as a player spell, so this follows that precedent
// rather than piloting from scratch. Real behavior confirmed by re-reading
// common/src/comp/ability.rs's `requirements_paid`: a `StaticAura` with
// `sprite_info: None` (this spell has no sprite -- it's a pure damage
// emanation, not a terrain effect) takes the plain `energy_cost` gate,
// same as any other ability; the `on_ground`-gated branch only applies
// when `sprite_info: Some(_)` (plant_growth's/rampart's case).
//
// Self-centered persistent-damage zone: sheet's own notes explicitly
// choose StaticAura ("the effect is a sustained zone anchored on the
// caster") even though the flavor text says the field "wraps around you"
// (implying it moves with the caster) -- StaticAura is anchored at cast
// position and does NOT follow the caster afterward (same simplification
// plant_growth.ron already documents: "persists after the caster walks
// away"). Accepted as-is, matching the sheet's own pre-declared modeling
// choice.
//
// No BuffKind deals literal "Thunder" damage -- `AuraBuffConstructor` only
// wraps a `BuffKind` (common/src/comp/aura.rs), and the closest generic
// HP-drain kind is `Bleeding` (`common/src/comp/buff.rs`:
// `HealthChangeOverTime { rate: -strength, tick_dur: Secs(0.5) }`).
// **Correction to a doc/impl mismatch found while researching this**:
// `BuffKind::Bane`'s own doc comment ("Lowers health over time...") reads
// like a damage-over-time debuff, but its actual `effects()` arm
// (buff.rs:962) is `Accuracy(-12 * nn_scaling(strength))` only -- no
// health-drain component at all. `Bane` was NOT used here for that reason;
// `Bleeding` is the real DPS primitive. Same category of documented
// flavor-vs-mechanism drift as this batch's other RONs (Explosion/
// GroundAoe/BasicBeam hardcoding their own DamageKind regardless of RON
// content).
//
// `duration: Some(1.0)` on the applied `Bleeding` tick (not the sheet's
// full 60s) is deliberate: it makes the debuff re-apply/refresh only while
// a target keeps standing inside the 3 m emanation (same short-refresh
// shape plant_growth.ron uses for its `DifficultTerrain` tick), so damage
// stops shortly after a target steps out, matching "creatures entering or
// starting their turn within it take damage" rather than a 60s DoT that
// outlasts leaving the zone. `aura_duration: Some(60.0)` matches the
// sheet's own `Concentration(60)` for how long the emanation itself
// persists.
StaticAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    energy_cost: 55.0,
    targets: OutOfGroup,
    auras: [
        (
            kind: Bleeding,
            strength: 5.0,
            duration: Some(1.0),
            category: Some(Magical),
        ),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(60.0),
    range: 3.0,
    sprite_info: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
